<title>USA: San Juan, N.M., $7.8 mln deal repriced, yld raised.</title>
<headline>San Juan, N.M., $7.8 mln deal repriced, yld raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Principal Financial Securities Inc said Thursday it repriced $7.755 million San Juan JCD, N.M., general obligation refunding bonds, raising the yield in 2004 to 5.05 percent from five percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>$7.755 MILLION</p>
<p>SAN JUAN JCD GO REFUNDING</p>
<p>FSA INSURED</p>
<p>MOODY'S: AAA (A1 UNDERLYING)</p>
<p>DATED 10/1/1996</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON 3/1/1997</p>
<p>DUE 9/1</p>
<p>NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>DELIVERY: 10/16/1996</p>
<p>ALL BONDS PRICED AT PAR</p>
<p>    9/1	     Amount	  Coupon</p>
<p>    Maturity	(million)	   (pct)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1997	    $0.845	  4.00</p>
<p>    1998	    $0.850	  4.30</p>
<p>    1999	    $0.675	  4.50</p>
<p>    2000	    $0.600	  4.65</p>
<p>    2001	    $0.650	  4.75</p>
<p>    2002	    $0.750	  4.85</p>
<p>    2003	    $0.800	  4.95</p>
<p>    2004	    $0.820	  5.05</p>
<p>    2005	    $0.870	  5.10</p>
<p>    2006	    $0.895	  5.20</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
